cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "To refer to the computational results, please cite this repository as below. Not peer reviewed. Produced by AI models under the direction of the repository owner (see AI_DISCLOSURE.md)."
title: "ramsey-cells: computation records and Lean/Comparator certificates for small two-colour graph Ramsey numbers (unreviewed)"
type: software
authors:
  - name: alejandrozarco
repository-code: "https://github.com/alejandrozarco/ramsey-cells"
abstract: >-
  Computation records for small two-colour graph Ramsey numbers from the cells of Radziszowski's Dynamic Survey
  DS1 (revision 18): colorings, cube-and-conquer refutations, encoders, independent checkers and certificates. For
  five cells the value is one Lean 4 theorem about 2-colorings, accepted by Comparator in the Lean kernel and in
  nanoda, resting on the three standard axioms and two named cake_lpr verdicts. AI-produced, not peer reviewed.
keywords:
  - Ramsey numbers
  - complete bipartite graphs
  - SAT solving
  - Lean 4
  - formal verification
license: MIT
references:
  - type: article
    title: "Small Ramsey Numbers"
    authors:
      - given-names: Stanisław P.
        family-names: Radziszowski
    journal: "Electronic Journal of Combinatorics"
    notes: "Dynamic Survey DS1, revision 18 (2026)"
    doi: "10.37236/21"
  - type: software
    title: "lrat-catcher"
    authors:
